Sparse native offload must retain the sliding-window history at the recurrent
state's replay boundary, not only at the prompt's final hash boundary.
With EAGLE-style block drop these positions differ by a block. Omitting the
leftmost SWA chunk makes joint lookup converge to zero even when the CPU tier
retains the full-attention prefix and its exact Mamba checkpoint.
Keep the existing prompt and shared-prefix tails, and add the aligned Mamba
replay boundary under sparse retention. Dense retention and group annotation
policy remain unchanged.

Kind: fix
What: retain SWA history at the earlier Mamba replay boundary under sparse offload
Upstream: HyperQwen issue #405
Cut-against: 0.33.0
Retires-when: upstream native offload retains every hybrid replay window

